ROMX $07
	"Roofs"
	"Tileset Data 2"
	; Kanto hack (MM-fix): "Extra Songs 1" used to sit here.  Mt. Moon's
	; tile-pair seal appends six cave metatiles ($42-$47, 96 B of metatile +
	; 24 B of collision) to "Tileset Data 2", which overflowed bank $07 by
	; 12 bytes.  The songs are reached through `dba` in the song table, so
	; the section is position-independent; it is now floated (the linker
	; picks a bank with room) rather than pinned.
ROMX $08
	"Clock Reset"
	"Tileset Data 3"
	; Kanto hack (M6 9q): "Egg Moves" used to sit here.  Celadon Gym's planter
	; maze appends 11 metatiles ($40-$4a, 176 B of metatile + 44 B of collision)
	; to TILESET_TRAIN_STATION in "Tileset Data 3", which overflowed bank $08 by
	; 177 bytes.  Egg-move data is read exclusively through GetFarWord/GetFarByte
	; with `BANK(EggMovePointers)` / `BANK("Egg Moves")` (engine/pokemon/breeding.asm),
	; so the section is position-independent.  Floating it builds fine, but it
	; is PINNED to bank $1c below (the emptiest bank) so the float pool -- and
	; with it where the floated "Tileset Data 5".."Tileset Data 13" land -- stays
	; exactly what it was before 9q.  Bank $01 reads 131 free bytes either way;
	; that figure is pre-9q (the "~140" in HANDOFF/9p findings is stale, spent by
	; the G1/P2 commits), and nothing 9q touches feeds bank $01.
ROMX $09
	"bank9"
